<title>SWEDEN: Astra posts 8 pct 9-mo profit rise.</title>
<headline>Astra posts 8 pct 9-mo profit rise.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish drug company Astra AB reports for the nine months ending September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			   9,850  vs  9,124</p>
<p> Sales				     28,137  vs 26,676</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)	     11.40  vs  10.76</p>
<p> Operating profit			 9,160  vs  8,487</p>
<p> Net interest income			708  vs    555</p>
<p> Currency differences	   CHARGE   13  vs     82 CREDIT</p>
<p> Net financial items	    CREDIT  695  vs    637 CREDIT</p>
<p> Minorities				     5  vs	0</p>
<p> Tax					  2,824  vs  2,492</p>
<p> Net profit				 7,026  vs  6,632</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuter poll of 14 analysts found an market consensus forecast for a pre-tax profit of 9.81 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
